Form the second composite \(g(f(x)) = \dfrac{1}{\sqrt{x} - 1}\). It requires \(x \geq 0\) for the square root and \(\sqrt{x} 
eq 1\) (i.e. \(x 
eq 1\)) so the denominator is non-zero.

