steps.explain:
Form \(g(f(x)) = \dfrac{1}{\sqrt{x}-2}\), which requires \(x \geq 0\) and \(\sqrt{x} 
eq 2\), i.e. \(x 
eq 4\). Its range: \(\sqrt{x} - 2\) covers \([-2, infty)\setminus{0}\), so the reciprocal covers \((-\infty, -\tfrac{1}{2}] \cup (0, infty)\).

